WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.405
Membership tier has a documented business order so
an ordinal encoder can preserve that rank

00:00:07.115 --> 00:00:12.974
The category list is written explicitly That matters
because software

00:00:13.001 --> 00:00:18.657
should not guess the intended order from
alphabetical sorting The resulting

00:00:18.683 --> 00:00:24.243
codes are compact and ordered But remember the
earlier caution some

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:29.006
models may treat the numeric gaps as equal so the
representation must fit the method

00:00:29.032 --> 00:00:30.111
and interpretation
